WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.315 --> 00:00:01.690
AJA: Today, I'm
going to show you

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.540
how to upload files to Google
Cloud Storage with Ruby.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:08.430
Here's the file
I want to upload.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:12.720
I'm using the Google
Cloud Storage gem.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.360
To use the gem, you need a
project and a service account

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.680
key.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:23.380
Here's my project, and I created
my service account key earlier.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.480
I'll be uploading via IRB.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.911
First, I require Google Cloud
and connect to my project.

00:00:32.556 --> 00:00:33.805
Now I create a storage object.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.450
Cloud storage calls
groups of files buckets,

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:39.701
so I need to create a bucket.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.610
Now I can upload my file
by calling creat file

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.670
in the bucket and passing it
the source and destination

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:47.169
filenames.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:50.732
It's that simple.

00:00:50.732 --> 00:00:52.690
To verify that the file
got uploaded correctly,

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:53.614
I can use the console.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.090
And there's the
picture I uploaded.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.220
I hope you found this helpful.

